The `release-binaries` workflow failed for tag 1.103 (2026-10-25, the latest run of that workflow) on x86_64 and aarch64, step "Verify binary". Run: `gh run view 40149008131 -R Getty/langertha-knarr --log-failed`.

    build-binary: not bundled, does not load: Langertha::Knarr (Can't locate namespace/autoclean.pm in @INC ...)
    build-binary: not bundled, does not load: Langertha::Knarr::Authorizer::Token (...)
    build-binary: not bundled, does not load: Langertha::Knarr::Handler::TokenRoutes (...)
    FAIL: knarr start: server exited
    Can't locate namespace/autoclean.pm ... at inc/lib/Langertha/Knarr/Authorizer/StaticKey.pm line 7.

`namespace::autoclean` is used by the modules but is neither installed in the build environment nor packed, so the release 1.103 has no working binaries attached.

## Steps

1. Check on `main` whether `namespace::autoclean` is declared in `cpanfile` (runtime requires) and reaches the binary build's module list; add it where it is missing.
2. Run the binary build and its verify step locally the way the workflow does.
3. Say on the card whether the 1.103 binaries should be rebuilt (`gh workflow run` on the tag) or whether the next release carries the fix; that choice is the maintainer's.

## Proof

The local binary starts (`knarr start` passes the verify script), and the workflow's next run is green.
